WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:11.273
First, advanced computing becomes affordable for everyone when expensive neural models act as a last resort behind fast local lookup tables, search indexes, and exact solvers.

2
00:00:11.613 --> 00:00:23.626
Second, compressing weights below one bit saves memory, yet unpacking them back to floating-point numbers at runtime wastes over eighty times more circuit-board energy than running packed integer logic directly.

3
00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:38.806
Third, one integer kernel checked by cryptographic hashes produces the exact same answer across processors, graphics cards, WebAssembly, hardware logic, and microcontrollers, halting immediately if a single weight changes.
